00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.450
Or were your parents just lying
to you out of convenience?

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.440
Well, the verdict, guess what?

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.970
They probably lied to you.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.350
There isn't a universal age
that is considered appropriate

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.790
for leaving children home alone,

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.860
only a few jurisdictions
even have firm rules

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.190
for how old the child must be

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.080
before they can stay at home unsupervised.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.180
For example, Maryland makes
it illegal to leave a child

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:03.250
under eight years old home alone,

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.710
and a babysitter for someone under eight

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.410
must be at least 13 years old.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.130
And believe me, Maryland
is not messing around,

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.240
even when it's not
technically against the law.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.610
Just ask the couple who let their,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.470
quote, "Free Range" kids aged 10 and 16

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.100
play unattended in a park,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.750
only to have Child Protective Services

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.290
called on them for neglect.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.170
The parents eventually won,

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.880
but not before their kids were interviewed

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:23.690
for hours by the local government,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.920
and after years of litigation.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.960
The local Maryland government
worse than Harry and Marv?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.720
- We know that you're in there
and that you're all alone.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.550
- I will let you decide on that one.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.210
And Illinois sets the bar even higher.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:38.580
It's considered abuse or neglect

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.307
to leave a minor under
the age of 14 home, quote,

00:02:41.307 --> 00:02:44.017
"Without supervision for an
unreasonable period of time

00:02:44.017 --> 00:02:45.877
"without regard to the
mental or physical health,

00:02:45.877 --> 00:02:48.000
"safety, or welfare of that minor."

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.720
But, of course, there is
some wiggle room here.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.020
What is considered an
unreasonable period of time?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.500
That implies that there is
a reasonable period of time

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.340
that you can leave a child unattended.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.090
And it's not unreasonable
to leave a child at home

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.870
if the child would essentially be safe,

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.703
but most states leave it

00:03:00.703 --> 00:03:02.810
to their local Department of
Health to create guidelines,

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:05.400
and these local authorities
consider many different factors.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.610
They consider the child's
age, maturity level,

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.280
how long the child's guardians are gone,

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.120
whether the house and
neighborhood are safe,

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.640
whether the child can easily contact

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.860
their parents or other adult,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.930
and most importantly, whether the child

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.290
can defend themselves
from two violent criminals

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.000
using nothing but toys,
leftover fishing equipment,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.270
and a tarantula.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.930
- You guys give up, or
you thirsty for more?

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.763
- So, there you have it,

00:03:25.763 --> 00:03:27.600
your parents lied to you, zero to one.

