But that takes us to the next thing

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:06.310
that our parents said was illegal,

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:08.670
it was that you can't
drive without wearing shoes

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.480
or you can't drive wearing flip flops,

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:11.980
I'm talking to you, Florida.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.270
Here, of course, is what you think

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.550
you look like driving barefoot,

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.960
compared to what your
parents think will happen

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.010
when you drive barefoot.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:20.100
So, the question, can you legally drive

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.130
without wearing shoes?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:24.100
Your parents thought the answer
was clear, absolutely not.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.640
And, of course, driver's ed instructors

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.190
also reinforced the idea that you have

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:28.440
to wear shoes to drive,

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.560
potentially just because they didn't

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.180
wanna smell your stinky feet,

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:34.250
but people have wondered whether
it was illegal for decades.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.270
To get to the bottom of this,

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:38.040
researcher Jason R. Heimbaugh
did a research project

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.990
in the early '90s on whether any state

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.940
actually made it illegal
to drive barefoot.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.380
He contacted every department
of motor vehicle office

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:45.290
in the United States.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:48.000
And it turns out that
none of the 50 States

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.890
or the District of Columbia
bared shoeless driving.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:53.520
Alabama does have a law
requiring you to wear shoes

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.930
while operating a motorcycle.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.190
If you're driving a
motorcycle, wear some shoes,

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.310
and also a helmet and a leather jacket.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.570
But even Alabama doesn't say anything

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.260
about wearing shoes in a car.

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:05.380
But before you celebrate
by burning your shoes

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.620
and running to your car,

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:08.340
there's one important
loophole to think about.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.080
The Illinois Director of Driving
Licensing and School Safety

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.200
told Heimbaugh that even without
a specific law on footwear,

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.180
police could still give a citation.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.470
Illinois Statutes 21-901 A and B

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.450
prohibit reckless and negligent driving.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.737
The director said, quote,

00:08:21.737 --> 00:08:24.047
"A driver charged under
these articles or any article

00:08:24.047 --> 00:08:26.937
"would have a right to trial
where the barefoot aspect

00:08:26.937 --> 00:08:28.880
"of the case might be disputed."

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:29.960
And so, the verdict,

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.180
there's no specific law
that seems to make driving

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:33.850
without your shoes on illegal.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.960
It's entirely possible

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.170
that some other motor vehicle law applies,

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:40.050
and doing so would be either
reckless or negligent.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:42.570
So, your parents might've
actually told the truth for once,

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:43.900
even though they didn't actually know it.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.010
And my verdict might surprise you,

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.730
but I think the police have a lot of laws

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.890
that they can use to give you a ticket,

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.290
just like the Grand Poobah

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.970
of the Illinois Driving Safety said.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.910
So, the bottom line, if
you get in an accident

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.170
while driving barefoot,

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.520
you might expect to be charged

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.750
with negligence, reckless driving

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.650
or operating a vehicle
in an unsafe manner,

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:00.150
so check your local ordinances

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.880
before defying your parents on this one.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.330
And as for flip-flops, all right,

